1
00:00:02,690 --> 00:00:11,634
On the corner of Maple and Ninth, everyone knows the rent is due on the first, and Mr. Grimm owns the first, the second, and every day after that.

2
00:00:11,894 --> 00:00:19,106
MIKA: An eviction notice... Grandma Rosa has lived here for forty years. They can't sell our building.

3
00:00:20,627 --> 00:00:26,147
Two hundred signatures. That was the number. And Mika had exactly one afternoon.

4
00:00:26,317 --> 00:00:29,609
MIKA: Run, Tommy! Every door, every floor, GO!

5
00:00:29,779 --> 00:00:31,695
TOMMY: Mika, wait for me! My legs are tiny!

6
00:00:31,865 --> 00:00:36,102
They raced through the alleys, up the stairwells, past every door on the block.

7
00:00:38,309 --> 00:00:47,705
JAYDEN: They say the block is fading, concrete cracking slow. But every crack we painted gold is a promise that we wrote. Sun goes down on Maple Street but the beat don't ever stop. Grimm can stack his coins up high, we hold the rooftop.

8
00:00:47,898 --> 00:00:56,964
ZOE: They came for the building, came for the view. But the heart of this city isn't concrete, it's me and you. Sign your name, stand in line, watch the whole block shine. One mic, one beat, one roof at a time.

9
00:00:57,157 --> 00:00:58,970
RICO: Everybody hands up! This block is OURS!
